{"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Reference","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference"],"anchor":"Reference"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" is an actor that conforms to "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and records every call it receives. Use it in ","type":"text"},{"code":"#Preview","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" blocks (where you don’t want real network traffic) and in tests (where you want deterministic assertions on what the plugin dispatched).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It does not import the Mixpanel SDK, so previews compile against it without configuring Mixpanel.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For usage examples, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Types","text":"Types","level":2},{"type":"heading","anchor":"docSwiduxMixpanelAnalyticsdocumentationSwiduxMixpanelAnalyticsMockMixpanelAnalyticsService","text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService``","level":3},{"code":["public actor MockMixpanelAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    public init(optedOut: Bool = false)","","    public nonisolated var isOptedOut: Bool { get }","    public func setOptedOut(_ optedOut: Bool) async","","    public private(set) var trackedEvents: [AnalyticsEvent]","    public private(set) var identifyCalls: [IdentifyCall]","    public private(set) var aliasCalls: [AliasCall]","    public private(set) var resetCount: Int","    public private(set) var flushCount: Int","    public private(set) var optOutCount: Int","    public private(set) var optInCalls: [OptInCall]","","    public struct IdentifyCall: Sendable, Equatable {","        public init(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue] = [:])","        public let userID: String","        public let properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]","    }","","    public struct AliasCall: Sendable, Equatable {","        public init(newID: String, previousID: String? = nil)","        public let newID: String","        public let previousID: String?","    }","","    public struct OptInCall: Sendable, Equatable {","        public init(distinctID: String? = nil, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]? = nil)","        public let distinctID: String?","        public let properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]?","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Recorded-state","text":"Recorded state","level":4},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"trackedEvents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — every ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"track(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", in dispatch order."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"identifyCalls","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — every "},{"code":"(userID, properties)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pair passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify(userID:properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"aliasCalls","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — every ","type":"text"},{"code":"(newID, previousID)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pair passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"alias(newID:previousID:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"resetCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — number of times "},{"code":"reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" was called."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"flushCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — number of times "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" was called."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"optOutCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — number of times ","type":"text"},{"code":"optOutTracking()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" was called.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"optInCalls","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — every ","type":"text"},{"code":"(distinctID, properties)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pair passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — current opt-out state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"isOptedOut","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is synchronous, like the real service’s. Every other accessor is ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so wrap reads in ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The record types have public initializers, so tests can build expected values: ","type":"text"},{"code":"#expect(await mock.identifyCalls == [.init(userID: \"user-1\")])","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":4,"text":"Consent","anchor":"Consent"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(optedOut:)"},{"type":"text","text":" stands in for the real service’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTrackingByDefault"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setOptedOut(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" routes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTracking()"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optInTracking()"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly as the real service does, so the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onConsentChange: { await service.setOptedOut($0) }"},{"type":"text","text":" wiring works against either. The mock sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOptedOut"},{"type":"text","text":" at once and records every call; it does not model the real service’s idempotence (a repeated opt-in is recorded again)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Determinism","level":4,"text":"Determinism","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The mock holds no buffers and adds no latency: every "},{"code":"track","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" records synchronously inside the actor. The plugin’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is still the right sync point for test assertions, since it drains the plugin’s own fire-and-forget task counter before the mock is queried.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The mock records "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"everything","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", including calls the real adapter drops — blank-"},{"code":"userID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and blank-","type":"text"},{"code":"newID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"alias","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" calls (see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), and calls made while opted out. A recording mock should never lose history; assert consent and validity at the call site, not by the absence of records."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockServiceReference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" — a recording "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mockservicereference"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}],"title":"Mock Service Reference","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"references":{"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsPlugin"},{"text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)"},{"type":"text","text":" calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mixpanel.initialize"},{"text":" internally so apps never need to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalyti